@startuml uc-inspect-configuration
!include _theme.iuml

state inspectConfiguration as "inspectConfiguration()" {

  state " " as RequestingResolved
  state " " as Resolving
  state " " as Presenting

  [*] --> RequestingResolved
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> asks what a repository will actually be
  governed by, rather than inferring it from a plan
  end note

  RequestingResolved --> Resolving
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> resolves the selection offline, with the same
  guarantee validateConfiguration() makes: no token, no network
  end note

  Resolving --> Presenting
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> prints the final resolved shape
  • which values survived precedence
  • values shaped like credentials are redacted
  • --format json wraps it in the versioned envelope
  end note

  Presenting --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> compares the resolved shape against what
  they expected to be managed
  end note
}

inspectConfiguration --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
exit 0
end note

inspectConfiguration -[#A78BFA]-> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
the layer each value came from is not
reported in this release: the resolver
does not track provenance per field
end note
@enduml
